# FINAL FANTASY RESONANCE (the full game; the demo is 4474710.env).
# No settings: it doesn't start in the bottle. It crashes 3 s in, inside its copy protection's
# code (Denuvo), before DirectX: that code hands the game's start-up a broken table, so a class
# name is read as a pointer (FFRS-Win64-Shipping.exe+0x11C6C18, "Widg"). Same place and value on
# every launch (Oct 10), and the same with the x86 emulator at its most exact:
#   FEX_X87REDUCEDPRECISION=0 FEX_MULTIBLOCK=0 FEX_TSOENABLED=1 (21:58), plus FEX_SMCCHECKS=full (22:13)
# It runs on a Steam Deck (a real x86 CPU, same SteamOS and Proton) and on x86 Linux generally,
# so the copy protection most likely turns down the emulated CPU / the VM. Hiding those from it
# is not something the bottle does. Even past that, it is DirectX 12 only.
